-- ==============================================================================-- QUERY TITLE       : Shallow Particle Size Distribution (GRAG)-- AUTHOR / EMAIL    : Richard Meredith / richard.meredith@geo-env.co.uk-- ORGANIZATION      : GeoEnvironmental Consulting Ltd-- PROJECT / TOOLS   : AGS Tools Project (FOSS)-- LICENSE           : GNU GPL v3 (GPL-compatible open-source)-- COMPATIBILITY     : QGIS 3.x (SpatiaLite / GeoPackage SQLite Provider)-- AGS VERSION       : AGS 4.0.x / 4.1.x-- SOURCE TABLES     : GRAG-- DESCRIPTION       : Filters particle size distribution (GRAG) grading test specimens to retrieve shallow results taken from depths less than or equal to 3.0m, ordered by exploratory hole location and specimen depth.-- ==============================================================================-- ==============================================================================-- ⚖️ GNU GPL v3 LICENSE & PROFESSIONAL DISCLAIMER -- ==============================================================================-- Copyright (C) 2026 GeoEnvironmental Consulting Ltd---- This SQL query is free software: you can redistribute it and/or modify-- it under the terms of the GNU General Public License as published by-- the Free Software Foundation, version 3 of the License.---- This code is distributed WITHOUT ANY WARRANTY; without even the implied -- warranty of MERCHANTABILITY or FITNESS FOR A PARTICULAR PURPOSE. See the-- GNU General Public License for more details <https://www.gnu.org/licenses/>.---- TO THE MAXIMUM EXTENT PERMITTED BY APPLICABLE LAW:-- 1. All implied terms, conditions, and warranties—including but not limited to --    implied terms of SATISFACTORY QUALITY, FITNESS FOR A PARTICULAR PURPOSE, --    and non-infringement of intellectual property—are hereby EXCLUDED.---- 2. The author and GeoEnvironmental Consulting Ltd shall not be liable for any --    direct, indirect, incidental, or consequential loss or damage (including --    but not limited to site engineering errors, financial loss, business --    disruption, or data corruption) arising from the use of, or reliance upon, --    the outputs generated by this script.---- 3. PROFESSIONAL RESPONSIBILITY (THE 'ENGAGE BRAIN' DIRECTIVE): --    This SQL query is a spatial processing tool, not a crystal ball. --    It does not replace professional, qualified human interpretation. Users are --    respectfully but firmly reminded to engage their brains (specifically ensuring --    cognition is in a forward gear) before executing this script or trusting its --    outputs. Trusting automated spatial interpolation blindly is a guaranteed --    recipe for causing expensive mistakes.---- NOTHING IN THIS DISCLAIMER SHALL LIMIT OR EXCLUDE LIABILITY FOR:-- (a) Death or personal injury resulting from negligence;-- (b) Fraud or fraudulent misrepresentation; or-- (c) Any other liability which cannot be excluded or limited under the laws of --     England and Wales.-- ==============================================================================SELECT *FROM GRAGWHERE CAST(SPEC_DPTH AS REAL) <= 3.0ORDER BY LOCA_ID, CAST(SPEC_DPTH AS REAL);